@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Method / document navigation. Scope-independent process/navigation; provider or runner examples are not MVP prerequisites.
title Resumefolio | Conflict analysis and negotiation
skinparam backgroundColor #101827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F1F5F9
skinparam hyperlinkColor #A9D0FF
skinparam dpi 216
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #9FB2CD
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #1C3453
 BorderColor #9FB2CD
 FontColor #F1F5F9
 DiamondBackgroundColor #49351C
 DiamondBorderColor #F2BA72
 StartColor #F1F5F9
 EndColor #F1F5F9
}
start
:Identify competing statements and exact sources;
:Compare actor, resource, state, operation and current decisions;
if (Genuine conflict in the same context?) then (yes)
 :Identify goals, evidence gaps and consequences;
 :Compare options, costs, risks and delivery effects;
 :Present recommendation and unresolved questions; <<#49351C>>
 if (Evidence sufficient and actual owner decision made?) then (yes)
  :Record selected / revised / rejected proposal,
  rationale, revision and actual decision date; <<#173B34>>
 else (not yet)
  :Keep dependent acceptance unresolved; <<#49351C>>
  :Record owner, next action and review gate;
  :Record any actual owner decision on a specific deferral;
 endif
else (context explains difference)
 :Clarify wording and link distinct contexts / records;
 :Preserve the existing accepted meaning;
endif
:Update affected requirements, criteria, models and traceability;
:Recheck consistency and retain remaining blockers;
stop
legend bottom
Recommendations are distinct from actual owner decisions.
Priority and sequencing do not silently remove agreed Version 1 scope.
No requirements baseline or product implementation is accepted by this workflow.
endlegend
@enduml
